# .trivyignore — scoped, justified suppressions for the trivy-fs gate.
#
# RULES (enforced by tools/lint-trivyignore.test.ts):
#   * One advisory ID per line (CVE-… or GHSA-…), optional `exp:YYYY-MM-DD`.
#   * Every suppression MUST carry a justification comment immediately above it.
#   * Suppress SPECIFIC advisory IDs only — never a severity class or `*`. A new,
#     unrelated CRITICAL/HIGH must still fail the gate.
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# tmp <= 0.2.3 — Path Traversal via unsanitized prefix/postfix (Dependabot #33).
# Transitive, DEVELOPMENT scope only (pulled in via the testcontainers/test
# toolchain — see pnpm-lock.yaml `dependency.scope: development`). It never ships
# in any runtime image: production Docker stages install with --prod and the
# `tmp` chain is dev-only. Zero production exposure. Tracked in
# .planning/deferred-items.md and memory project_dependabot_tmp_path_traversal.
# Remove once the upstream dep that pins `tmp` releases a patched range.
# exp:2026-08-31 — re-evaluate; if `tmp` is still pinned, extend with a fresh
# justification rather than letting this silently persist.
CVE-2026-44705
